  "title": "More ways to make images and inspect model options",
  "summary": "A community-heavy day brought new MCP tools, 24 catalog apps, animated GIF output, and a clearer Enter dashboard.\n\nGPT Image 2.6 Flare gained PNG, WebP, and animated GIF output, with frame and duration controls for GIFs. The models API now lists supported resolutions where available. FLUX Schnell keeps the requested aspect ratio when it adjusts image sizes, and Play preserves linked video settings when a model alias resolves. A Gemini 4 Carbon PR has no confirmed release date, so it is not included in the user-facing changes.\n\nThe Research MCP gained arXiv search and paper lookup, plus Crossref search and DOI lookup. Other MCP additions cover voice isolation and changes, npm download counts, Go and Packagist packages, MAC addresses, Wikimedia's On This Day feed, fractions, text diffs, and SemVer ordering. Agents now keep separate Computers across runs. Catalog and documentation updates make the tools easier to find.\n\nTwenty-four community apps joined the catalog. They range from model-comparison tables and agent phone calls to science simulations, hidden-message postcards, writing tools, and games where AI agents draw or plan heists. The README's recent-apps list rotated as entries arrived; those rotations did not remove apps from the catalog.",
  "pr_count": 64,
